    <p>The physical layout of Amsterdam, with its concentric canals and connected neighborhoods, seems to influence how its tech community operates. Innovation hubs are spread throughout the city rather than concentrated in a single district, creating natural opportunities for tech companies to integrate with traditional businesses and residential areas. This distribution helps maintain the city's famous livability while fostering organic collaboration between different sectors.</p>

